# The split screen scene, which F7 in mygame cycles to (see docs/rendering/frame.md and docs/world/scenes.md#streaming): two
# players on a streaming world of five tiles, in two views side by side, each with its own follow camera, HUD and audio
# listener. Player 1 walks with W, A, S and D and Space, player 2 with the arrow keys and right Control or Enter, or each
# with the gamepad of its number. C or a gamepad's Y claims the overview camera for a few seconds, which shows one full-screen
# view and then gives the split back (see scripts/split_screen.luau). A hidden floor under every tile keeps the players
# up while a tile streams in. Positions are raw World_Position values in units of 2^-24 m, so 2516582400000000000 is
# 1.5e11 m. The editor writes this file; see docs/editor/document-and-scenes.md#scenes.
